# API, Security & Entitlements (Permanent)

## Request context

Every authenticated business-scoped request must resolve:

1. `user` (from token)
2. `business` (from **path** `:businessId` — canonical) — membership required
3. `subscription` + entitlements for that business (when billing exists)

Optional header `X-Business-Id` may mirror the active business for clients; **authorization still uses path `businessId`** on scoped routes. Never trust a header alone without membership check.

Reject if membership missing or subscription not in `{trial, active, grace}` for mutating ops.

## EntitlementGuard (required)

Central Nest service + Guard; used on every mutating/export route:

- `assertBusinessWritable(businessId)`
- `assertModule(businessId, 'module.map')`
- `assertCan(businessId, 'export.pdf')`

UI mirrors the same codes from `/businesses/:businessId/entitlements`.

Editor + Corporate modules wire-up:

- Palette lists only allowed module blocks; locked modules shown with upgrade CTA
- Document / template body save and PDF enqueue assert modules via `documentCollectRequiredModuleCodes` (map, orgChart, timeline, gallery, gated repeater/`when` sources) → **403** `ENTITLEMENT_MODULE_REQUIRED`
- Module content pages (projects/map/org/timeline/gallery) show billing upgrade CTA when locked
- Catalog seed includes all `MODULE_ENTITLEMENT_CODES` as paid add-ons (not in `plan.core` base)

## Billing integrity

- Trial grant is transactional with first Business create; set `trial_consumed` atomically.
- Payment webhooks: **idempotent** (store gateway ref unique); activate subscription only after verified success.
- Never delete invoices/payments; append-only ledger mindset.
- Module changes recalculate entitlements without wiping documents.
- Route money/license through **edition adapters** (`SAAS` platform billing vs `SELF_HOSTED` license + optional local gateway). EntitlementGuard stays edition-agnostic.
- PostgreSQL holds payments/invoices/subscriptions; Redis backs webhook idempotency locks when useful.

## Security checklist (every feature)

- OTP brute-force protection + cooldown.
- Upload: MIME/extension allowlist, size limits, re-encode images; treat SVG as dangerous.
- XSS: escape in PDF HTML pipeline; sanitize rich text.
- IDOR: authorize `businessId` on every show/update/delete (PostgreSQL and MongoDB).
- CSRF as applicable; CORS locked to known web origins.
- Rate-limit export and OTP endpoints.
- Audit log for: login, business create, plan change, payment, export, delete.

## API shape

- JSON:API-ish or consistent `{ data, meta, errors }` — pick one style and keep it.
- Errors: machine `code` + human `message` (localizable; client maps `code` for fa/en).
- List endpoints: pagination + default sort; never return entire tenant tables.
- Idempotency-Key header supported on payment/subscribe endpoints when feasible.
- **Documentation:** keep `docs/api/` in sync on every route add/change/delete.
- **OpenAPI source of truth:** hand-maintained `docs/api/openapi.yaml` is canonical. Nest `@nestjs/swagger` may mirror for `/api/docs` UI but must not diverge — update YAML in the same change as routes.
